Error ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- test.js:15:1

Cannot call `x.foo` because in property `foo`: `() => number` [1] is not exactly the same as `() => number` [2].
[incompatible-type]

The above-mentioned two types must be the same because property `foo` is invariantly typed. To fix the error,
- Either annotate object literal [3] with `{foo: () => number, x: number}` [4]
- Or make property `foo` in object type [4] readonly. See
https://flow.org/en/docs/faq/#why-cant-i-pass-a-string-to-a-function-that-takes-a-string-number.

   test.js:15:1
   15| x.foo(); // unfortunate error, but makes sense: the union receiver is incompatible with both branches
       ^

